The table structure information is ({database name: {schema name: [table name]}}): 
{'MITELMAN': {'PROD': ['CYTOCONVERTED', 'KARYCLONE', 'MOLBIOLCLINASSOC', 'CYTOGEN', 'KARYABNORM', 'REFERENCE', 'AUTHORREFERENCE', 'CYTOCONVERTEDLOG', 'KARYBIT', 'KODER', 'MOLCLINBREAK', 'MOLCLINGENE', 'RECURRENTNUMDATA', 'CYTOGENINV', 'CYTOBANDS_HG38', 'CYTOGENINVVALID', 'KARYBREAK', 'MOLCLINABNORM', 'RECURRENTDATA']}}

Some few-shot examples after column exploration may be helpful:
Query:
--Description: look-up the textual definition of morphology code 3111 (breast cancer)
SELECT 
    k."Kod", 
    k."Kortnamn", 
    k."Benamning"
FROM MITELMAN.PROD.KODER k
WHERE k."KodTyp" = 'MORPH'
  AND k."Kod" = '3111'
LIMIT 20;
Answer:
Kod,Kortnamn,Benamning
3111,CA ad,Adenocarcinoma
Query:
--Description: look-up the textual definition of topography code 0401 (adenocarcinoma)
SELECT 
    k."Kod", 
    k."Kortnamn", 
    k."Benamning"
FROM MITELMAN.PROD.KODER k
WHERE k."KodTyp" = 'TOP'
  AND k."Kod" = '0401'
LIMIT 20;
Answer:
Kod,Kortnamn,Benamning
0401,Breast,Breast
Query:
--Description: preview adenocarcinoma (topology = 0401) cases in the clinical table – removed non-existent column "InvNo"
SELECT 
    g."RefNo",
    g."CaseNo",
